{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.NZBarEvenVolumeFace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.NZBarEvenVolumeFace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.nzReVolume_phase_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.nzReVolume_phase_odd","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/NZBarEvenVolumeFace.lean#L49-L52","doc":"The Volume-deviation face is **odd** in the phase (the CS face is the even\none) — the quadrature signature that identifies which face is which. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.nzReVolume_real_ray","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.nzReVolume_real_ray","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/NZBarEvenVolumeFace.lean#L42-L47","doc":"**Real ray ⇒ Volume-deviation off (corrected).** `sin 0 = 0`: on the real\nsubstrate ray the Volume face is the undeformed `Vol` exactly. The old\n`nzReVolume r 0 = (√3/2)r²` (and its `≠ 0` / `> 0` corollaries) belonged to the\nCS face. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.nzReVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.nzReVolume","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/NZBarEvenVolumeFace.lean#L37-L40","doc":"The **bar-even Volume-DEVIATION face** of the NZ meridian deformation\n(corrected quadrature): `Re 𝔙 − Vol = −(√3/2)·r²·sin(2φ)`. Odd in `φ`;\nvanishes identically on the real ray. ","signatureChunk":0}]}